# Recipe command surface

Native GSD workflows under `.cursor/get-shit-done/workflows/` hardcode `/gsd-*`
commands in their handoff text. Those strings are upstream and cannot be
patched. Translate them before showing a next step to the operator.

**Never recommend a `gsd-*` command as the operator's next action.** When a
native GSD workflow emits one, substitute the recipe wrapper:

| Native GSD emits | Recommend instead |
|---|---|
| `gsd-new-project`, `gsd-import` | `recipe-onboard` |
| `gsd-map-codebase`, `gsd-graphify build`, `gsd-ingest-docs` | `recipe-bootstrap-knowledge` |
| `gsd-plan-phase N` | `recipe-plan-phase N` |
| `gsd-execute-phase N [--wave W]` | `recipe-run-phase N [--wave W]` |
| `gsd-verify-work N`, `gsd-audit-milestone`, `gsd-audit-uat` | `recipe-verify-feature N` |
| `gsd-code-review N`, `gsd-ship N` | `recipe-review-ship N` |
| `gsd-progress`, `gsd-next`, `gsd-health` | `recipe-status` |

The wrappers add gating the native commands skip — planning-policy compliance
checks, `depends_on` reminders, and `execute_started`/`execute_complete` Jira
lifecycle events through the idempotent sync ledger. Recommending the native
command silently drops tracker sync.

If the correct next command is unclear, run
`.gsd-recipe/scripts/recipe-next.sh` and print its output verbatim rather than
guessing.

## When `gsd-*` is still correct

- The operator explicitly asked about or for a native GSD command.
- Pointing at `gsd-help` for native depth beyond the recipe catalog.
- Explaining which native skill a recipe wrapper delegates to.
- Authoring or editing recipe templates, GSD workflows, or docs that describe
  the delegation.

